-- an application whose function is a λ written out is its body with the argument put in: the
-- checker gives a λ a type only against one expected, so a call of a definition, whose code is
-- unfolded in place, is checked as what it computes to. The argument is then checked where the
-- body uses it and nowhere else: an argument the body drops is not checked. Carrying each
-- definition's type beside its code (a definition's type as code is not obtainable in this module)
-- would check the call as a call
nk-beta : NkTm → NkTm → NkTm
nk-beta (nk-lam b) a = nk-put b #0 a
nk-beta f a = nk-app f a
